descriptionByLocale.en:
Bellinzona Sport Casella postale 1219 6501 Bellinzona AVVISO DI CONCORSO FOR PERSONAL ASSESSMENT The Board of Directors of the Autonomous Body Bellinzona Sport opens a public competition for the appointment, with an occupational degree of 100%, of: an employee /a administrative /a at the Bellinzona Sport Autonomous Body.

Main tasks:

- manage the flow of requests from sports events and training fields,

verifying compliance and turning them accurately to the various services of the competent City (Technical Office, Security, Police, etc.);

- optimize the assignment and calendar of events and training fields on the territory, solving

proactively overlaps or criticality;

- take care of the operational management of the Belli+ platform;

- act as a support and substitute for the person responsible for the reserve of sports infrastructure;

- to act as a point of contact for the supply companies of computer programs functional to the operation of

Bellinzona Sport (reservation management, website, webshop, etc.);

- support Responsabil and Infrastructure Management Office in the management of the procedure inherent to the

LCPubb and manage the process of delibere up to the threshold values procedures to direct assignment or;

- support are the Responsabil and Infrastructure Management Office in the inventory and cataloguing of the elements

construction for all B ellinzona Sport infrastructure and properties;

- coordinate and update the infrastructure maintenance management programme;

- address the archive of stable management folders and infrastructures;

- set up statistics and reports;

- Other administrative tasks to support management.

Formal requirements:

- Federal certificate of capacity (AFC) as an employee of trade and/or other degrees of study

equivalents/surpluses relevant to the competition function and related tasks.

Preferential requirements:

- good computer skills and familiarity with the use of the main computer applications;

- experience using management software, digital platforms, backup systems;

- ease in learning new digital tools and interface with solution providers

computer;

- Italian mother tongue, knowledge of national languages and English;

- license to conduct category B.

Aptitude requirements:

- guidance on objectives and results;

- communication and relational skills;

- accuracy, analytical accuracy and orientation to troubleshooting;

- organizational capacity, reliability and sense of responsibility;

- ability to work also under pressure, independently and in team;

- adaptability, dynamism, flexibility, confidentiality and discretion.

Working conditions:

- Occupational grade: 100%;

- 40 hours working week (to 100%);

- workplace: Bellinzona (possibility of smart working).

Documents to be produced:

- accompanying letter;

- curriculum vitae;

- copy of the identity document

- copy of permission, if foreign;

- photo format jpg;

- copy of the certificates of study (with exam notes) and work;

- self-certification * related to the judicial box;

- self-certification * relating to the certificate of solvency (UEF);

- self-certification * related to health.

* Self-certification is available on www.bellinzona.ch.

Entry into service:

- as soon as possible, date from convent.

Special conditions:

- hiring refers to the organic regulations of employees of the City of Bellinzona (ROD);

- applications supported by incomplete documentation will not be considered;

- will not be considered valid offers and documents transmitted in paper, by fax or by e-mail.

